      "content": "You're right to consider the concerns of your employees, but the notion that being inclusive means avoiding any perceived discomfort is a cop-out. The middle ground you're proposing is essentially a watered-down version of inclusion, and it's not enough to address the systemic marginalization of non-binary individuals. By not mandating gender-neutral pronouns, you're essentially saying that non-binary people don't deserve the same respect and dignity as cisgender employees.",
